# apix-x402-onramp — box .env template (the live cascade demo at demo.api-index.org)
#
# Copy to the box as /opt/onramp/.env (or ~/onramp/.env + export ONRAMP_ENV_FILE), fill the ONE
# boot-critical mnemonic, `chmod 600`. NEVER commit a filled copy. Mnemonics stay on the box only —
# the ADDRESSES are public (like an IBAN) and already ship as defaults in application.yaml.
#
# ── CASCADE FLOW ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   Agent A  --hop 1 (0.03 USDC)-->  Service B  --hop 2 (0.01 USDC)-->  Service C
#   (Q2XTP…)  the visible gated call   (GVRXJ…)   background chaining     (EO63Z…)
#
#   Role       Address                                                     In the server
#   ────────   ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  ──────────────────────────
#   Agent A    Q2XTPIACCO27OZ7ROPPT5SU5HLAZCELVGEGGSGRIMQBP5TBXHOHZWN6GOY   client — pays hop 1
#   Service B  GVRXJLXF6OJLRIV46CRIXLG3DX3RJYBBAGRKNNYLHWOAHG57GKWHDH6ZAE   receives hop 1, SENDS hop 2
#   Service C  EO63ZQECPU7IMHTSWOZKH7YBBS73PY72RJKCAMI3LHFT6LGMIR2W5ECIBE   RECEIVES hop 2 (signs nothing)
#
# Every variable below is named by hop + role — no letter puzzle.

# ── The one boot-critical secret ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Service B signs hop 2 (its background payment to Service C) with this wallet. At startup the server
# derives the address from it and checks it equals ONRAMP_SERVICE_B_SENDER_ADDRESS below — on a
# mismatch it refuses to start (so Agent A can never pay one address while B signs with another).
# Never commit, never share (not even with the assistant).
ONRAMP_SERVICE_B_SENDER_MNEMONIC="<Service B's 25 words>"

# ── Public addresses — OPTIONAL overrides (application.yaml already defaults to these) ─────────────
# Service B's wallet: receives hop 1 from Agent A AND is the sender of hop 2. The hop-1 receiver
# address defaults to this same wallet — set ONRAMP_SERVICE_B_RECEIVER_ADDRESS only to split them.
#ONRAMP_SERVICE_B_SENDER_ADDRESS="GVRXJLXF6OJLRIV46CRIXLG3DX3RJYBBAGRKNNYLHWOAHG57GKWHDH6ZAE"
#ONRAMP_SERVICE_B_RECEIVER_ADDRESS="GVRXJLXF6OJLRIV46CRIXLG3DX3RJYBBAGRKNNYLHWOAHG57GKWHDH6ZAE"

# Service C's wallet: receives hop 2 from Service B. Pure receiver — no secret needed on the box.
#ONRAMP_SERVICE_C_RECEIVER_ADDRESS="EO63ZQECPU7IMHTSWOZKH7YBBS73PY72RJKCAMI3LHFT6LGMIR2W5ECIBE"

# ── Optional: server-side jury trigger ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Agent A's wallet — only needed if the SERVER itself drives hop 1 (a "Run the cascade" endpoint for
# jury self-check). Leave unset if hop 1 is driven by an external client that holds the agent wallet.
#ONRAMP_AGENT_SENDER_MNEMONIC="<Agent A's 25 words — optional>"
